WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.939
This is the National Mall in

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.080
Washington, D.C.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.559
More than 25 million people

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.560
visit annually. At

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.949
lunchtime on any given

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.078
day, hungry tourists spill

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:17.100
out onto the streets.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.619
Majeed Naim, the owner of the

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.599
food Truck Chicken Friendly, is

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.600
feeding them

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.249
from his spot in front of the

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.529
National Museum of American History

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.299
as he competes against dozens of

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.799
others in a parking free for all.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.048
Location is everything.

00:00:39.049 --> 00:00:41.099
To keep their prized

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.169
spots, vendors park dummy

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.279
cars overnight.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.599
These trucks offer better value

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.009
than the pricey cafes at the

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.240
Smithsonian Museums.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.859
Right now, customers are at the

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.719
National Mall and they're screaming

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.009
out for more food options.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.779
Attorney Justin Pearson directs the

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.609
National Street Vending Initiative

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.709
at the libertarian legal nonprofit,

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.449
the Institute for Justice.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.679
So it makes sense that food trucks

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.179
try to provide those food options so

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.439
that the food trucks can stay in

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.970
business and not lose their dream.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.629
The diversity is incredible.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.489
The food is so well cooked.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:23.719
You can see they really poured their

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.709
hearts into it.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.569
The prices are extraordinary.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.189
You can't beat it.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.539
These food trucks really have an

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.099
impact on people around here.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.269
And, you know, I just think they're

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.270
good for the community.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.259
They face another challenge.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.260
These guys.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.609
We are like struggling a little bit

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.319
with the tickets every day.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.899
Sometimes $200 each day, $300

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.209
each day. So it's not like easy

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.210
here.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.929
Sometimes the police bother

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.129
us. Sometimes.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.839
I mean, not sometimes, all the time

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.249
we get that like a ticket.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.499
Selling food from a truck along the

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.969
National Mall is technically

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.409
illegal.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.269
That mattered less before COVID

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:12.169
because there were other

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.219
neighborhoods where they were

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.300
allowed to serve lunch.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.139
So what was appealing

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.359
was the gratification

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.279
you get when you have 50 people

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.929
in line that are just going to try

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.879
your food and they love it.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.279
The pandemic obviously closed

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.499
all of the office buildings.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.689
Trucks then ha d to find other

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:33.690
places to vend.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.939
The mall became the only spot in

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.859
D.C. with significant lunchtime

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.860
for traffic.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.669
So we walk here and

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.579
National Mall for just the tourists.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.049
Before name was serving chicken

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.879
fingers. He raised the live chickens

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.199
on a farm in Egypt.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.729
He eventually saved enough to buy

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.730
his own truck.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.259
We hope everything goes back to like

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.189
a normal. I don't have nothing else

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.099
to do besides this, only the

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.100
foot truck business.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.909
Meanwhile, the fines rack up.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.439
Last year the city collected

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.449
$467,000

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.709
in parking tickets along with them

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.710
all.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.009
What's happening at the National

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.299
Mall is a real shame.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.979
Customers are being ripped off by

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.869
overpriced food sold

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.699
at the museum's cafeterias, and

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.619
that problem is directly a result

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.269
of the lack of competition.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.009
It's ultimately a problem of

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.389
jurisdiction.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.279
Nobody seems to want to be

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.839
take charge on the enforcement.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.729
Patrick Rathbone, who's the owner of

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.739
the big cheese truck used to serve

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.119
the D.C. lunch crowd.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.219
Now he focuses exclusively

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.810
on catering and special events.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.539
So the roads, our D.C.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.489
jurisdiction as from the sidewalk on

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.689
is National Park Service.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:49.619
They think the National Park

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.449
Service, maybe, should be doing

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.279
enforcement. So there's inter-

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.469
bureaucracy like apathy,

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.029
I guess. Nobody wants to be in

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.919
charge of actually taking care of of

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.920
the trucks down there.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.389
The National Park Service has

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.249
resisted calls from lawmakers to

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.569
make vending legal there.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.889
I think there has to be a meeting

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.299
between the D.C.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.669
folks and the National Park Service.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.679
DC can say we can solve the

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.019
parking in the illegal vending

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.179
piece of it, but if we don't solve

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.399
the transaction side of things

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.409
that's in your hands, Park

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.760
Service, it's not going to work.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.939
With no compromise in sight, food

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.619
truck operators remain stuck in the

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:44.620
middle.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.269
And millions of visitors keep coming

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.159
to the mall every year looking for a

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.809
delicious and affordable lunch.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.979
With officers waiting nearby.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.579
I see the future kind of like

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.861
a little bit difficult because

00:05:09.862 --> 00:05:11.779
we still get like bothered

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:13.939
from park police and

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:14.749
for the tickets.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.759
So I was thinking I would have

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.289
to leave this business to get

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.599
something else but for now, I'm

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.949
still in this business to see what's

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:22.950
going on.

